 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Footsteps for the way out, geometric for «عفوا غفورا», growth for «مراغما كثيرا وسعة», a house for «من بيته», an hourglass for shortening the prayer. No death drawn (100:21-22). 101:12-17 «إن خفتم…» is not glossed (Al-Muyassar adds that shortening is allowed in safety too; As-Sa'di's wording differs), so no side is taken. STAGING v4: 98-99: in a town, the truly oppressed (a group of 4, so it includes a woman as the verse names men, women and children; not uncountable: a crowd behind rocks would read as people in hiding or troops) sit and lower their heads on 98:8 (unable to find a way); geometric for the pardon, ending before the emigrant walks. 100: an emigrant traveller appears on 100:1 (he is not on stage during 98-99) and leaves on 100:2 and walks out of the town; growth plate for the refuge and plenty, house plate for leaving his home; wide shots only (no close-up on the lone traveller); nothing is drawn for death (100:21-22): he does not fade or leave there. 101: believers travelling in the desert with a camel pray where they stand on 101:9-11 (the hourglass plate for shortening); during 101:15-23 (the disbelievers as enemies) the camera turns to the empty horizon; no enemy, weapon or fear gesture is drawn."
 },
